## Creating Projects from Command Line

Once you have .NET 8 SDK installed, you can create any missing projects using these commands:

### Web API Projects

```bash
# Compliance API
cd src/Services/Compliance/Compliance.API
dotnet new webapi -n Compliance.API

# Allocation API
cd src/Services/Allocation/Allocation.API
dotnet new webapi -n Allocation.API

# TradeBooking API
cd src/Services/TradeBooking/TradeBooking.API
dotnet new webapi -n TradeBooking.API

# TradeOrchestrator API
cd src/Services/TradeOrchestrator/TradeOrchestrator.API
dotnet new webapi -n TradeOrchestrator.API

# FundData API
cd src/Services/FundData/FundData.API
dotnet new webapi -n FundData.API

# ReferenceData API
cd src/Services/ReferenceData/ReferenceData.API
dotnet new webapi -n ReferenceData.API
```

### Class Library Projects

```bash
# Domain projects
cd src/Services/Compliance/Compliance.Domain
dotnet new classlib -n Compliance.Domain

cd src/Services/Allocation/Allocation.Domain
dotnet new classlib -n Allocation.Domain

cd src/Services/TradeBooking/TradeBooking.Domain
dotnet new classlib -n TradeBooking.Domain

cd src/Services/FundData/FundData.Domain
dotnet new classlib -n FundData.Domain

# Infrastructure projects
cd src/Services/Compliance/Compliance.Infrastructure
dotnet new classlib -n Compliance.Infrastructure

cd src/Services/TradeBooking/TradeBooking.Infrastructure
dotnet new classlib -n TradeBooking.Infrastructure

# Shared projects
cd src/Shared/Shared.Contracts
dotnet new classlib -n Shared.Contracts

cd src/Shared/Shared.Common
dotnet new classlib -n Shared.Common

cd src/Shared/Shared.Infrastructure
dotnet new classlib -n Shared.Infrastructure
```

### Add NuGet Packages

After creating projects, add required packages:

```bash
# Example: Compliance.API
cd src/Services/Compliance/Compliance.API

dotnet add package Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi --version 8.0.0
dotnet add package Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.CSharp.Scripting --version 4.8.0
dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.SqlServer --version 8.0.0
dotnet add package Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore.Tools --version 8.0.0
dotnet add package Swashbuckle.AspNetCore --version 6.5.0
dotnet add package Serilog.AspNetCore --version 8.0.0
```

### Add Project References

```bash
# Example: Compliance.API references
cd src/Services/Compliance/Compliance.API

dotnet add reference ../../../Shared/Shared.Contracts/Shared.Contracts.csproj
dotnet add reference ../../../Shared/Shared.Common/Shared.Common.csproj
dotnet add reference ../Compliance.Domain/Compliance.Domain.csproj
dotnet add reference ../Compliance.Infrastructure/Compliance.Infrastructure.csproj
```

## Verifying Your Setup

After creating all projects:

```bash
# From solution root
dotnet restore
dotnet build

# Should show successful build for all projects
```

